<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Oct auto output up 2 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Oct auto output up 2 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian automobile output over January to October rose two percent on a year ago to 719,000, though truck output declined 13 percent to 110,000, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The committee data for vehicle production showed the following figures:</p>
<p>		     Jan-Oct 1996 percent	Oct 1996 output</p>
<p>		     number of   change on    percent change on:</p>
<p>		     vehicles    yr earlier    Sept 1996  Oct 1995</p>
<p> Automobiles     719,000	 +2	     +22	   +15</p>
<p> Trucks	    110,000	-13	     +12	    +7</p>
<p> Buses		31,800	 -6	     +27	   +16</p>
<p>		    Month/month</p>
<p>		     change by</p>
<p>		   manufacturer</p>
<p> GAZ		     +9</p>
<p> UAZ		    +13</p>
<p> AvtoVAZ		+22</p>
<p> Kamaz		  +27</p>
<p> Zil		   +200</p>
<p> Izhmash		-24</p>
<p> AZLK(Moskvich)    closed</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
